Findings (recon against crates/compiler/src/parser + crates/runtime,
recorded here so the GREEN implementation has the real contract):

1. String literals are double-quoted ONLY and have NO escape mechanism
   (parser/lexer.rs read_string stops at the next '"'). The conftest
   _BASE example query `MATCH Service WHERE name == 'settlement' ...`
   does NOT lex — a lying example that must be fixed.
2. MATCH predicates address properties only — there is no KOID
   addressing in the text grammar.
3. TRAVERSE is outbound-only, one rel_type per clause, DEPTH optional
   (default 1, 0 rejected at compile). A mixed-rel two-hop path cannot
   be expressed in one query — it composes as two chained queries.
4. RETURN * after TRAVERSE yields RowSet::Traversal, which tool_aikoql
   renders as {"results": []} (query.rs matches only Objects/Scored) —
   a traverse query MUST project a field (the Project op loads the KOs).
5. Integral literals lower to Value::Int (mod.rs kq010) and cross-type
   comparison is fail-closed: ints render as integers, floats as
   decimals; negative numbers ('-' does not lex) and scientific
   notation ('e' lexes as an ident) are unrepresentable.
6. Ident names (type/property/rel) must match [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_:]*
   and must not be keywords (MATCH/WHERE/... lex as tokens).

